---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 15</p>
  <h1>Past-time <em>expressions</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Put every past event on the line from now backward. Three small families do most of the work: <span class="ex">yesterday morning</span>, <span class="ex">last night</span>, <span class="ex">two years ago</span>. Learn how each family behaves, then answer the question every past-simple conversation asks: <span class="ex">When did it happen?</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">yesterday · last · ago</span>
    <span class="tag">when + past simple</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read four sentences about last month.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Three families: yesterday, last, ago.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, type, and build sentences.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Talk about your week and your past.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">This is the vocabulary partner of your past simple lesson. Every expression here answers one question: <span class="ex">When did it happen?</span> <span class="ex">Yesterday</span> looks one day back, <span class="ex">last week</span> names the week before this one, and <span class="ex">two years ago</span> counts back from now.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="moved">moved</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="move">move</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Wednesday">Wednesday</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Monday">Monday</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Last year we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="moved" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to a new apartment. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(previous grammar lesson · past simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My English class starts <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> six o’clock. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 · prepositions of time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The day after Tuesday is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Wednesday" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A0 · days of the week)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Four anchors in past time</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Four pictures, four distances into the past. Say each one aloud in a full sentence: <span class="ex">I checked my email an hour ago.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/sunrise.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">yesterday morning</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/moon.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">last night</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/clock.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">an hour ago</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/calendar.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">in 2020</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read Marta’s update</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“I started this job <strong>two years ago</strong>. <strong>Last month</strong> my team moved to a new office, and <strong>yesterday morning</strong> we had our first meeting there. It went well, so <strong>last night</strong> I slept very well.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">two years ago</span>. Where does <span class="ex">ago</span> sit: before the time or after it? Is that the same in your language?</li>
      <li>Marta says <span class="ex">last month</span>, not <span class="ex">the last month</span>. Which little word disappears after <span class="ex">last</span>?</li>
      <li>She says <span class="ex">yesterday morning</span> but <span class="ex">last night</span>. Why not <span class="ex">yesterday night</span>? English simply never says it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: read the cue, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Parts of yesterday take <b>yesterday</b>. Whole past periods take <b>last</b>, with no <b>the</b>. To count back from now, put <b>ago</b> after the time.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="yesterday">yesterday</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="last">last</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the last">the last</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="ago">ago</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="before">before</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I saw Dana <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="yesterday" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> morning. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the morning of the day before today)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We watched a movie <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="last" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> night. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not yesterday night)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I started this job two years <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ago" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(after the time, not before it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I was really busy <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="last" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> week. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(no the)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She graduated <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 2021. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(year · A1 preposition)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>He called me an hour <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ago" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(count back from now)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: three families</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The <strong>yesterday family</strong> names the day before today and its parts. It works alone, with no preposition:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>the yesterday family</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>yesterday</b></td><td>the day before today</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>yesterday morning</b></td><td>the early part of that day</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>yesterday afternoon</b></td><td>the middle part of that day</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>yesterday evening</b></td><td>the late part of that day &nbsp;<span class="contraction">for the night, say last night</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>the day before yesterday</b></td><td>two days back from today</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The <strong>last family</strong> names the most recent complete period: the night, week, month, or year just before this one. There is <strong>no the</strong>: <span class="ex">last week</span>, never <span class="ex">the last week</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>the last family</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>last night</b></td><td>the night before today &nbsp;<span class="contraction">this replaces yesterday night</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>last week</b></td><td>the week before this one</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>last month</b></td><td>the month before this one</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>last year</b></td><td>the year before this one</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>last Monday</b></td><td>the most recent Monday before today</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The <strong>ago family</strong> measures distance back from now. Name the amount of time, then add <span class="ex">ago</span>. <strong>Ago always comes after the time</strong>, never before it:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>the ago family</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>an hour ago</b></td><td>one hour back from now</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>two days ago</b></td><td>two days back from now &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not before two days</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>three weeks ago</b></td><td>three weeks back from now</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a long time ago</b></td><td>far back, exact distance unknown</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">Yesterday</span> points at one specific day. <span class="ex">Last week</span> points at one specific period. <span class="ex">Two days ago</span> doesn’t name anything; it <strong>measures</strong> backward from this moment.</li>
      <li>The families can describe the same moment: if today is Wednesday, <span class="ex">the day before yesterday</span>, <span class="ex">last Monday</span>, and <span class="ex">two days ago</span> can all point at the same day.</li>
      <li>All three families work alone: no <span class="ex">in</span>, no <span class="ex">on</span>, no <span class="ex">at</span>, and no <span class="ex">the</span> before <span class="ex">last</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>A timeline you can point to</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Read the timeline from top to bottom: each row is one step further into the past. Point at a row and say a true sentence about it.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>how far back</th><th>what to say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>earlier today</b></td><td>this morning · an hour ago · at nine o’clock</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>one day back</b></td><td>yesterday · yesterday morning · yesterday afternoon · last night</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>two days back</b></td><td>the day before yesterday · two days ago</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>earlier this week or last week</b></td><td>last Monday · three days ago · last week</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>months back</b></td><td>last month · three weeks ago · in May</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>years back</b></td><td>last year · two years ago · in 2020 · a long time ago</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>in, on, at still work in the past</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Your A1 prepositions of time did not retire. They mark past time at exactly the same jobs:</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>The old jobs, unchanged</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">in</span> + year or month: <span class="ex">She graduated <strong>in 2021</strong>. We met <strong>in May</strong>.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">on</span> + date or day: <span class="ex">My interview was <strong>on May 12</strong>. He arrived <strong>on Monday</strong>.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">at</span> + clock time: <span class="ex">The movie started <strong>at eight o’clock</strong>.</span></li>
      <li>But the three families work alone: <span class="ex">last week</span> (not <span class="ex">in last week</span>), <span class="ex">yesterday</span> (not <span class="ex">on yesterday</span>).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Where does the time expression go?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Time expressions usually come <strong>at the end</strong> of the sentence: <span class="ex">We watched a movie <strong>last night</strong>. I sent the report <strong>an hour ago</strong>.</span></p>
  <p>To set the scene, move the expression <strong>to the front, with a comma</strong>: <span class="ex"><strong>Last night,</strong> we watched a movie. <strong>Two years ago,</strong> we moved here.</span></p>
  <p>To ask about past time, use <span class="ex">when</span> with the past simple: <span class="ex"><strong>When did</strong> you move here? <strong>When did</strong> she call?</span> A short answer can be just the time expression: <span class="ex">Two years ago. Last night.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the right word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint"><b>yesterday</b>, <b>last</b>, and <b>ago</b> work alone. Keep <b>in</b> for years and months, <b>on</b> for dates and days, <b>at</b> for clock times.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="yesterday">yesterday</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="last">last</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="ago">ago</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I called my sister <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="last" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> night. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the night before today)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We met ten years <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ago" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(count back from now)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Did you watch the game <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="yesterday" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> afternoon? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(part of the day before today)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>She finished college <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 2019. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(year)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>My interview was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> May 12. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(exact date)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The movie started <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> eight o’clock. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clock time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>He sold his car a month <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ago" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(after the time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>I was in Miami <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="last" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> week. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the week before this one · no the)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the missing word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">One word per gap. Decide first which family the sentence needs, then type.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I didn’t sleep well <input class="answer-input" data-answer="last" aria-label="answer 1" /> night.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We talked about it the day before <input class="answer-input" data-answer="yesterday" aria-label="answer 2" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She moved to Chicago six months <input class="answer-input" data-answer="ago" aria-label="answer 3" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="When" aria-label="answer 4" /> did you start your job?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>He was born <input class="answer-input" data-answer="in" aria-label="answer 5" /> 1998.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I sent you the email an hour <input class="answer-input" data-answer="ago" aria-label="answer 6" />.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="we moved here two years ago">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the answer to “When did you move here?”</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Count back from now, and remember where <span class="ex">ago</span> goes. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="ago">ago</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="we">We</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="two">two</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="moved">moved</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="years">years</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="here">here</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i saw her last friday">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the sentence with the last family</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The most recent Friday before today. No <span class="ex">the</span>, no <span class="ex">on</span>. Build it, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="friday">Friday</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="saw">saw</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="last">last</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="her">her</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Two classic errors travel with this vocabulary in almost every language. Learn the repairs as chunks:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>don’t say</th><th>say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>yesterday night</b></td><td><b>last night</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">the night belongs to the last family</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>before two days</b></td><td><b>two days ago</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">ago comes after the time</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>the last week</b></td><td><b>last week</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">no the</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>on yesterday</b></td><td><b>yesterday</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">no preposition</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="yesterday" data-fix="I called you last night." data-why="English has yesterday morning, yesterday afternoon, and yesterday evening, but not yesterday night. For the night before today, say last night.">
    <h3>Drill 5: repair the night</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong, then say the corrected sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="called">called</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="yesterday">yesterday</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="night">night.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="before" data-fix="She left an hour ago." data-why="To measure back from now, name the time first and put ago after it: an hour ago, two days ago. Before does not do this job in English.">
    <h3>Drill 6: repair the measurement</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong, then say the corrected sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="left">left</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="before">before</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="an">an</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hour">hour.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7: move it, then answer it</h3>
    <p>Say the full new sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> We watched a movie last night. &nbsp;→&nbsp; move the time expression to the front</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Last night, we watched a movie.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Two years ago, we moved here. &nbsp;→&nbsp; move the time expression to the end</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We moved here two years ago.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> When did you see Maria? &nbsp;→&nbsp; the most recent Friday</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I saw her last Friday.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> When did the meeting start? &nbsp;→&nbsp; 9:00</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It started at nine o’clock.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> When was Leo born? &nbsp;→&nbsp; 1998</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He was born in 1998.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> When did they arrive? &nbsp;→&nbsp; one hour back from now</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They arrived an hour ago.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Catching up with Nadia</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Hi Tomas! Sorry for the slow reply. It was a crazy month. We moved to a new apartment three weeks ago, and last week I started a new job downtown. Yesterday morning I had my first big meeting, and last night we finally unpacked the last box. The day before yesterday my parents visited to see the place. Let’s get coffee soon. Are you free on Friday?”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You followed a real catching-up message across three weeks of past time.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="three weeks ago">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. When did Nadia move to the new apartment?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three weeks ago">three weeks ago</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="last week">last week</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="yesterday morning">yesterday morning</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="she started a new job">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What did Nadia do last week?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="she started a new job">She started a new job.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="she had her first big meeting">She had her first big meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="she unpacked the last box">She unpacked the last box.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="last night">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. When did they unpack the last box?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="last night">last night</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the day before yesterday">the day before yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three weeks ago">three weeks ago</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Last week in three sentences:</b> Say three true sentences about last week, each with a different time expression. <span class="ex">Last week I worked a lot. On Wednesday I had a long meeting. Last Friday I saw my parents.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your starting point:</b> Say when you started your job or your studies, two ways: once with the ago family and once with a year. <span class="ex">I started my job three years ago. I started in 2023.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Interview the teacher:</b> Ask the teacher three questions with <span class="ex">When did you…?</span> and listen for the time expression in each answer. <span class="ex">When did you move to your city? When did you start teaching? When did you last travel?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Yesterday, hour by hour:</b> Walk through your day yesterday from morning to night. <span class="ex">At seven o’clock I woke up. Yesterday morning I answered emails. Yesterday afternoon I met a client. Last night I cooked dinner.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A long time ago:</b> Tell a short childhood memory. Start with <span class="ex">A long time ago…</span> and use at least two more past-time expressions as the story moves.</div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the system</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For the night before today, I say ______. After <strong>last</strong> I never add the word ______. The word <strong>ago</strong> comes ______ the time: two years ______. For years I use <strong>in</strong>, for dates I use ______, and for clock times I use ______.”</p>
    <p>Then answer with a real time expression: <span class="ex">When did you start learning English?</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can place past events with yesterday, last, and ago, keep in, on, and at for years, dates, and clock times, and answer When did you…? naturally.">
    <h3>Final quiz: choose the right expression</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="last">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. I saw that movie ___ night.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="last">last</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="yesterday">yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ago">ago</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="ago">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. We got married ten years ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ago">ago</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="before">before</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="last">last</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="yesterday">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. I had coffee with Dan ___ morning.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="yesterday">yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="last">last</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ago">ago</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="in">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. She started her new job ___ 2022.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at">at</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="on">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. My interview was ___ May 12.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at">at</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="When did you move here?">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which question is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When did you move here?">When did you move here?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When you moved here?">When you moved here?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When did you moved here?">When did you moved here?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I was in Rome last week.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I was in Rome last week.">I was in Rome last week.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I was in Rome the last week.">I was in Rome the last week.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I was in Rome in last week.">I was in Rome in last week.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Last night">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. ___, we stayed home and watched a movie.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Last night">Last night</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Yesterday night">Yesterday night</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The last night">The last night</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
